<title>THAILAND: NPC says protected against baht losses.</title>
<headline>NPC says protected against baht losses.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's National Petrochemical Plc's U.S. dollar denominated revenues offer the company a natural hedge against the baht's weakness against the greenback, the firm said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>National Petrochemical has around $225 million in long term loans, the firm said in a statement. Sales from its main olefins products are in dollars, it added.</p>
<p>The baht has depreciated around 15 percent since it was floated last Wednesday, ending a 13-year period in which it was linked to a basket of currencies dominated by the U.S. dollar.</p>
<p>The baht's weakness has raised fears about Thai firms' ability to repay foreign denominated debt.</p>
<p>($1 = 29 baht)</p>
</text>
